! Fcc platinum with spin-orbit coupling, for a spinor ultracell on an augmented
! dataset. `pt-soc-nosym.in` with ecutrho brought down to 4 ecutwfc and the
! k-grid raised so that a two-cell ultracell at kgrid = (2, 2, 2) folds onto it.
!
! This is the only committed fully relativistic LDA dataset -- every other one
! (Co, I, Ni, the other two Pt) is PBE, which an ultracell refuses by name -- so
! it is the one cell where `fcoef` is not the identity and the spin-orbit
! sandwich inside the displaced tables is exercised at all. Silicon's two
! datasets are scalar-relativistic, where that sandwich collapses.
!
! starting_magnetization = 0.0 makes this nspin_mag = 1: spinor wavefunctions
! carrying no magnetization, so the four Pauli components reduce to the charge
! one. That is deliberate -- it isolates the sandwich from the spin blocks, and
! the spin blocks are measured on silicon where the sandwich is trivial.
!
! ecutrho = 4 ecutwfc rather than the dataset's own dual, which an ultracell
! refuses; the comparison against a real supercell is at the same pair on both
! sides and is like for like, and the absolute energy is not converged in
! ecutrho.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 7.42, nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    lspinorb = .true., noncolin = .true., starting_magnetization = 0.0,
    ecutwfc = 30.0, ecutrho = 120.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'mp', degauss = 0.02,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Pt  195.08  Pt.rel-pz-n-rrkjus.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS alat
 Pt  0.0  0.0  0.0
K_POINTS automatic
 4 2 2 0 0 0
